---
/**
 * Privacy Policy.
 *
 * Rewritten when Google Analytics was added. The earlier version was accurate
 * for a site that set no cookies, loaded no third-party script and measured
 * nothing -- it said so in as many words, which is exactly why it could not
 * survive the tag. Sections that described the absence of analytics now
 * describe what the analytics does.
 *
 * Every technical statement below was checked against the built output:
 * gtag.js is on all 47 pages, the proposal form is still a mailto: that
 * submits nothing to us, and Google is the only third party the browser
 * contacts.
 *
 * Metadata is passed to BaseLayout directly rather than added to
 * src/lib/page-meta.js. resolvePageMeta() returns its not-found record for any
 * key it does not know, and BaseLayout only treats that as noindex when the
 * page supplies no title of its own. Passing one keeps this page indexable and
 * self-canonical without touching the fixed-page table.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/sections/PageHero.jsx";

const EFFECTIVE = "16 September 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  metaKey="privacy-policy.html"
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How PT. Immer Asia Corporation handles information on the Immersia website: what Google Analytics measures, the cookies it sets, the proposal form that composes an email in your own mail application, and your rights under Indonesian data protection law."
>
  <PageHero label="Legal" title="Privacy Policy" />

  <article class="articlebody">
    <p class="lead">
      This website is a set of static pages. It measures visits with Google
      Analytics, loaded through Google Tag Manager, which sets cookies in your
      browser. The proposal form sends nothing to us — it composes an email in
      your own mail application. This page explains both.
    </p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>Effective {EFFECTIVE}.</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>PT. Immer Asia Corporation</strong>, trading as Immersia, is an
        impact advisory and capacity-building firm. Our office is at Jl. Sepat
        No.43, Kebagusan, Ps. Minggu, Jakarta Selatan 12520, Indonesia.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are the data controller for the information described on this page.
        For anything in this policy, write to <a href="mailto:info@immersia.id"
          >info@immersia.id</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics and tag management</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics 4 (measurement ID G-0RFC45PYLN) to understand
        how the site is used — which pages are read, how visitors arrive, and
        roughly where in the world they are. We use it to decide what to write
        and what to fix. We do not use it to identify you, and we do not
        combine it with anything else we hold.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google Analytics runs on every page of this site and collects, among
        other things:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Pages viewed, and the order and timing of those views</li>
        <li>How you arrived — a search engine, a link, or a direct visit</li>
        <li>
          Device and browser information, such as screen size, operating system,
          and language
        </li>
        <li>
          Approximate location, derived from your IP address at country or city
          level. Google Analytics 4 does not log or store full IP addresses.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We also use Google Tag Manager (container GTM-TM9VB4ZQ) to load and
        manage these measurement tags. Tag Manager is a container: what it
        loads is configured in Google's console rather than written into this
        website, so the set of tags on this site can change without the site
        itself changing. If we add a tag that collects anything beyond what is
        described here, we will update this page.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google LLC processes this data on our behalf, and that processing takes
        place on Google's infrastructure, which is located outside Indonesia.
        Google's own handling of the data is governed by its privacy policy at
        <a
          href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">policies.google.com/privacy</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Google Analytics sets cookies in your browser so that repeat visits from
        the same device are counted as one visitor rather than several. These
        are named <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_&lt;container id&gt;</code>.
        They contain a randomly generated identifier for the browser, not a name
        or an email address.
      </p>
      <p>
        These are the only cookies this site sets. Tag Manager itself sets
        none. There are no advertising cookies, and nothing on this site is used
        to build a profile of you or to target you elsewhere.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can refuse or delete them in your browser's settings, or install
        Google's own opt-out add-on at
        <a
          href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout</a
        >. Refusing them does not affect anything you can read or do here.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>No advertising or tracking pixels.</strong> Google Analytics,
          loaded through Google Tag Manager, is the only measurement tool on this
          site, and Google is the only third party the page contacts.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No accounts.</strong> There is nothing to register for and no
          password is ever asked for.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No selling or sharing.</strong> We do not sell your
          information, rent it, or pass it to anyone for their own marketing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No embedded content.</strong> There are no embedded videos,
          maps, calendars, or widgets. The one frame on the page is Tag
          Manager's fallback for browsers with JavaScript turned off: it is
          hidden, has no content you can see or interact with, and does nothing
          when JavaScript is on.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The proposal form</h2>
      <p>
        The form on our <a href="/request-proposal.html">Request Proposal</a> page
        does not send anything to us over the internet. When you press submit,
        your browser assembles your answers into an email message and opens it
        in your own mail application. Nothing is transmitted until you send that
        message yourself, and you can edit or discard it first.
      </p>
      <p>
        This means the form data never reaches a server of ours. There is no
        database behind it and no submission is recorded anywhere on this site.
      </p>
      <p>The message your browser composes contains the fields you filled in:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Organization name</li>
        <li>Contact person</li>
        <li>Work email</li>
        <li>Phone or WhatsApp, if you provide it</li>
        <li>Service of interest</li>
        <li>Background or challenge</li>
        <li>Expected outputs, if you provide them</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Email you send us</h2>
      <p>
        Once you send that message — or write to us directly — it arrives in our
        inbox at info@immersia.id. From that point it is ordinary business
        correspondence. We use it to reply to you, to prepare a proposal if you
        have asked for one, and to keep a record of the engagement.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not use it for marketing lists, and we do not sell or rent it.
      </p>
      <p>
        We keep correspondence for as long as the enquiry or the working
        relationship it belongs to remains live, and afterwards for as long as
        our records and legal obligations require. You can ask us to delete it
        sooner; see <em>Your rights</em> below.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
      <p>
        This website is hosted by Vercel. Like any hosting service, Vercel
        receives the network requests your browser makes in order to serve the
        pages back to you. Those requests carry your IP address and browser
        information, which Vercel processes to deliver the site and to protect
        it from abuse, and retains according to its own policy. This happens for
        every website you visit, on any host; it is not something this site
        adds.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not read those logs, analyse them, or build profiles from them.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other services</h2>
      <p>
        Our pages link to WhatsApp, Instagram, and LinkedIn. Those are links,
        not embeds: nothing is loaded from them while you read our site, and
        nothing about your visit is shared with them unless you click through.
      </p>
      <p>
        Once you follow such a link you are on someone else's service, under
        their privacy policy and not ours.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under Indonesia's Personal Data Protection Law (Undang-Undang No. 27 of
        2022 on Pelindungan Data Pribadi), you may ask us for access to the
        personal data we hold about you, ask us to correct it, ask us to delete
        it, object to how we are using it, or withdraw consent you have given.
      </p>
      <p>
        In practice this concerns two things: the email correspondence we hold —
        the messages you have sent us and our replies — and the analytics data
        described above.
      </p>
      <p>
        Write to <a href="mailto:info@immersia.id">info@immersia.id</a> to
        exercise any of these. We may need to keep some records where we have a
        legal obligation to do so, and we will say so if that applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This website is addressed to organizations and their staff. We do not
        knowingly collect personal data from children.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we change how this site works — by adding another measurement tool,
        an embedded service, or a form that submits to a server — we will update
        this page before that change goes live, so that what it says stays true
        of the site you are actually using. This page was last rewritten when
        Google Analytics was added.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        PT. Immer Asia Corporation, Jl. Sepat No.43, Kebagusan, Ps. Minggu,
        Jakarta Selatan 12520, Indonesia. Email
        <a href="mailto:info@immersia.id">info@immersia.id</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        See also our <a href="/terms-of-use.html">Terms of Use</a> and
        <a href="/disclaimer.html">Disclaimer</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
